The function `tegra_emc_prepare_timing_change` contains the reversed logic for checking the DLL status in the EMRS register (represented by `emc_mode_1`). Specifically, lines 523-528 show:

	if ((last->emc_mode_1 & 0x1) == (timing->emc_mode_1 & 0x1))
		dll_change = DLL_CHANGE_NONE;
	else if (timing->emc_mode_1 & 0x1)
		dll_change = DLL_CHANGE_ON;
	else
		dll_change = DLL_CHANGE_OFF;

In DDR3, bit 0 of EMRS1 is 0 for DLL Enable and 1 for DLL Disable. The code incorrectly maps a high bit (1) to `DLL_CHANGE_ON` and a low bit (0) to `DLL_CHANGE_OFF`, which is the exact reversed logic described in the vulnerability root cause.

