	else if (timing->emc_mode_1 & 0x1)
		dll_change = DLL_CHANGE_ON;
	else
		dll_change = DLL_CHANGE_OFF;

In DDR3, EMRS1 bit A0 (bit 0 of `emc_mode_1`) is 0 when DLL is enabled and 1 when DLL is disabled. The code incorrectly identifies DLL as turning ON (`DLL_CHANGE_ON`) when the bit is high (1), which is the reversed logic described in the root cause.

